==Battleground==
*15 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 3~4 seconds<sup>90f~120f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
*1 [[Ms. Sign]] spawns after 176.67 seconds<sup>5,300f</sup>.
*20 [[Assassin Bear]]s spawn after 183.33 seconds<sup>5,500f</sup>, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Like the stage [[Last Gang]], the main gimmick is that you should beat the stage before 183 seconds, if not, the Assassin bears would spawn and destroy you. [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]] works to get rid of the Wall Doges quickly. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is also a solid choice, as it can get rid of the constant Trolly Blogger spam, while dealing damage to Nyandam, with a Time Between Attacks of only 2.13. Courier Cat at lv50 needs to hit Nyandam approximately 65 times in order to kill him.  Bring [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist Cat]] too, or any anti-red uber you have, to quicken the process. You can also stack Courier if you manage to stack a lot of cats that can knockback reds, ([[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Catley]], [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Bean Cats]], etc..) which will cause Nyandam to be pinned to the base without being able to attack your stack.

